<!-- ═══ LEARNING ONLINE ═══ -->
<div class="section section--alt" id="learning-online">
  <div class="section-narrow">

    <h2 class="reveal">Learning online</h2>

    <div class="faq-item reveal">
      <h3>Can Qigong really be learnt properly online?</h3>
      <p>Yes, and for one-to-one tuition it works remarkably well. Every session is taught live over Zoom, Microsoft Teams or Google Meet, with me watching you throughout. This is not a video course with a forum attached: you practise, I watch, and I correct you as you go.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item reveal">
      <h3>How can posture be corrected if the teacher isn't in the room?</h3>
      <p>By insisting on it. You set your camera so your whole body is visible, and I'll ask you to turn to the side, to the front and sometimes to the back, so I can check each alignment from the angle that shows it best. I'm strict about this, and would rather spend most of a session on a single detail than let a poor habit settle in. Many students find remote work sharpens their own awareness, because you learn to find and feel an alignment yourself rather than being physically pushed into it.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER 1 - file: img/faq-online-1.jpg -->
    <figure class="faq-media reveal">
      <img src="/img/faq-online-1.jpg" alt="Posture being checked during a live online Qigong session" loading="lazy" onerror="this.closest('figure').style.display='none'">
      <figcaption>Posture checked from the side during a live online session</figcaption>
