    <div class="faq-item reveal">
      <h3>Is it a group class or one to one?</h3>
      <p>The online courses are one to one. The pace, the emphasis and the order of work are shaped around your body, your level and your goals rather than around a fixed syllabus.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item reveal">
      <h3>How long is a session?</h3>
      <p>90 minutes, with full-length posture checks rather than brief demonstrations.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item reveal">
      <h3>What do I need at home?</h3>
      <p>Very little. A clear space of roughly two metres by two metres, a device with a camera that can be placed a few metres back so your whole body is in shot, a reasonably stable connection, and loose clothing that doesn't hide what your hips and knees are doing. Bare feet or flat, thin-soled shoes are ideal. A quiet spot where you won't be interrupted helps more than anything technical.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item reveal">
      <h3>I'm in a different time zone. Is that a problem?</h3>
      <p>No. Sessions are arranged flexibly around your schedule and time zone, and your course begins when you're ready rather than on a fixed intake date.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item reveal">
      <h3>What if my connection drops mid-session?</h3>
      <p>It happens occasionally and it's easily dealt with. Time lost is made up, either later in the same session or in the next one.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item reveal">
      <h3>Do I get any written material?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Full notes and diagrams are provided for every form, so you're never relying on memory alone between sessions.</p>
    </div>

